# Combinators on arrays and maps

`map`, `filter`, and `fold` are collection methods. The block is a delayed
function. `fold` takes the seed first. Target prints through `wchntConsole`.

On an array the block sees one element. On a map it sees the key and the value.
`filter` keeps the same collection type. `map` on a map keeps the keys and
replaces the values. `fold` types `acc` from the seed: `0` is Int, `""` is
String, `[:Summary 0 0]` is Summary.

## Schema

```
Team = [Player]/players {String : Int}/scores
Player = String/name Int/score
Summary = Int/total Int/count
```

## Construction

```
[:Team
  [:Array/Player
    ["Ada" 3]
    ["Bob" 0]
    ["Cy" 5]
  ]
  {String:Int "Ada":3 "Bob":0 "Cy":5}
]
```

## Methods

```
Team::names = { players.map({ p | p.name }) }

Team::scorers = { players.filter({ p | p.score > 0 }) }

Team::total = { players.fold(0, { acc, p | acc + p.score }) }

Team::boosted = { scores.map({ k, v | v + 1 }) }

Team::hot = { scores.filter({ k, v | v > 0 }) }

Team::sum = { scores.fold(0, { acc, k, v | acc + v }) }

Team::stats = { players.fold([:Summary 0 0], { acc, p | [:Summary (acc.total + p.score) (acc.count + 1)] }) }

Team::joined = { players.fold("", { acc, p | acc.concat(p.name) }) }
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var team = TeamAssemblage.factory();
    wchntConsole.println("names");
    wchntConsole.println(team.names());
    wchntConsole.println("scorers");
    wchntConsole.println(team.scorers());
    wchntConsole.println("total");
    wchntConsole.println(team.total());
    wchntConsole.println("boosted");
    wchntConsole.println(team.boosted());
    wchntConsole.println("hot");
    wchntConsole.println(team.hot());
    wchntConsole.println("sum");
    wchntConsole.println(team.sum());
    wchntConsole.println("stats");
    wchntConsole.println(team.stats());
    wchntConsole.println("joined");
    wchntConsole.println(team.joined());
}
```
